@host = http://localhost:5041

### 1. Register
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Test Employee",
  "email": "employee1@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### 2. Who am I
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me

### 3. Logout
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout

### 4. Login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "employee1@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### 5. Login with a wrong password
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "employee1@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword1"
}

### 6. Categories (log in first)
GET {{host}}/api/categories

### 7. Create a ticket
POST {{host}}/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Printer on floor 2 is jammed",
  "description": "The printer shows a paper jam error and will not print.",
  "categoryId": 6,
  "type": "Incident",
  "priority": "High"
}

### 8. My tickets
GET {{host}}/api/tickets/my

### 9. My tickets filtered by status
GET {{host}}/api/tickets/my?status=Open

### 10. My tickets with a search word
GET {{host}}/api/tickets/my?search=printer

### 11. One ticket
GET {{host}}/api/tickets/1

### 12. Invalid category
POST {{host}}/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Bad category test",
  "description": "This should be rejected by the server.",
  "categoryId": 999
}